  "worked_solution": "Remember that $y=|x-h|+k$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nThe function $y=|x-4|+3$ has $h=4$ and $k=3.$ Therefore, it is a translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $4$ units *right* and $3$ units *up*.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192632/assets/a0a914b0961f151f2b05b18e30feabb304915c016ee9552251130aa740a4e715.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the coordinates of the minimum point are $(4,3).$",
